From ae4f4631ea2a176acd58598f428df24772cf3cab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:18:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dashboard): show resume wait notice for implicit
 active-session resume

When a /chat socket connects with no ?resume= param, pty_ws can fall back
to the channel's active-session file and announce that replay with a
{"type":"resume"} control frame (#93518). ChatPage then sets
resumeHydrating for the fresh --resume PTY, which boots just as blank as
an explicit resume. The render gate still required Boolean(resumeParam),
so on this path (for example reconnecting after the keep-alive PTY was
reaped) the "Please wait while the conversation loads..." notice stayed
hidden and the user saw an empty terminal with a blinking cursor.

resumeHydrating is only set when a resume target exists (URL param or
control frame), so the extra URL-param guard added nothing except
excluding the implicit path. Drop hasResumeTarget from
shouldShowResumeLoadingOverlay and gate on hydrating alone.

Add a ChatPage test: a fresh chat shows no notice, the control frame
shows it, and the first PTY output hides it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
